---
title: "Full Row Editing"
description: "Edit all cells in a row simultaneously using full row editing mode in the $framework Data Grid."
---

Configure the grid to enter and exit edit mode for an entire row at once.

Try these interactions in the example below:

-   Double-click any cell to start editing the entire row.
-   Press {% kbd "⇥ Tab" /%} / {% kbd "⇧ Shift" /%} & {% kbd "⇥ Tab" /%} to move between cells on the editing row.
-   Press {% kbd "↵ Enter" /%} or click outside the row to stop editing.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Full Row Editing" name="simple-full-row-editing" exampleHeight=400 /%}

The example above uses the following configuration:

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    editType: 'fullRow',
};
```

## Custom Cell Editors

If using custom cell editors, the cell editors will work in the exact same way with the following additions:

-   `focusIn`: If your cell editor has a `focusIn()` method, it will get called when the user tabs into the cell. This should be used to put the focus on the particular item to be focused, e.g. the `textfield` within your cell editor.
-   `focusOut`: If your cell editor has a `focusOut()` method, it will get called when the user tabs out of the cell. There is no intended use for this; it's just there to complement the `focusIn()` method.
-   Events: When a row stops editing, the `cellValueChanged` event gets called for each column and `rowValueChanged` gets called once for the row.

Note that `focusIn()` and `focusOut()` are only called when the user tabs between cells — not when double-clicking to start editing or pressing {% kbd "↵ Enter" /%} to stop.

## Full Row Edit Example

The example below uses the API to start editing a cell and demonstrates a custom editor on the **Price** column, along with two additional column configurations:

-   The **Price** column uses a custom `NumericCellEditor` with `focusIn()` and `focusOut()` implemented. Both methods are logged to the console when triggered.
-   The **Read Only** column is not editable, so when the row enters edit mode the cell cannot be changed. It remains focusable via {% kbd "⇥ Tab" /%}.
-   The **Suppress Navigable** column is skipped entirely during {% kbd "⇥ Tab" /%} / {% kbd "⇧ Shift" /%} & {% kbd "⇥ Tab" /%} navigation.
-   The button starts editing line two via the API. Even though a single cell is targeted, the entire row enters edit mode.
-   `cellValueChanged` and `rowValueChanged` events are logged to the console.

{% gridExampleRunner title="Full Row Editing" name="full-row-editing" exampleHeight=527 /%}

## Full Row Edit and Popup Editors

Full row editing is not compatible with popup editors. Opening a separate popup for each cell in a row simultaneously would create confusing UX and unmanageable navigation complexity.

You can still show a popup from within your in-cell editor however the responsibility of showing and hiding it belongs with your editor. Use the grid's focus events to hide the popup when the user tabs or clicks out of the cell.
